WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.600
Hi there!

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.136
Have you ever had an argument about what's fair, like

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:05.804
who gets the last cookie?

00:00:05.804 --> 00:00:08.005
Grown-ups have disagreements too.

00:00:08.005 --> 00:00:11.074
And sometimes they need help sorting them out.

00:00:11.074 --> 00:00:12.875
That's what a court is for!

00:00:13.575 --> 00:00:16.732
A court is a special place where people go to

00:00:16.732 --> 00:00:20.379
solve big problems in a fair way, by following rules

00:00:20.379 --> 00:00:21.852
that everyone shares.

00:00:21.852 --> 00:00:23.815
These rules are called laws.

00:00:24.515 --> 00:00:27.317
In charge of the courtroom is the judge.

00:00:27.317 --> 00:00:29.978
The judge is like a referee in a game.

00:00:29.978 --> 00:00:34.039
They make sure everyone follows the rules, and that nobody

00:00:34.039 --> 00:00:35.580
gets treated unfairly.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.961
Each side gets a lawyer.

00:00:37.961 --> 00:00:41.603
A lawyer is a helper who knows lots about the rules.

00:00:41.603 --> 00:00:45.245
They speak up for their side and explain their story

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.856
as clearly as they can.

00:00:47.556 --> 00:00:51.157
Witnesses are people who saw or know something important.

00:00:51.157 --> 00:00:54.883
They promise to tell the truth, then they answer questions,

00:00:54.883 --> 00:00:57.599
so everyone can learn what really happened.

00:00:58.299 --> 00:01:00.067
Sometimes there is a jury.

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:03.534
A jury is a group of ordinary people from the town.

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:07.952
They listen carefully to everything, then work together to decide

00:01:07.952 --> 00:01:09.584
what they think is true.

00:01:10.284 --> 00:01:13.579
The most important idea in court is fairness.

00:01:13.579 --> 00:01:15.775
Both sides get a turn to talk.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.313
Everyone must listen.

00:01:17.313 --> 00:01:20.901
And the decision should be based on facts, not on

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:23.902
who is richest, loudest, or most popular.

00:01:24.602 --> 00:01:26.228
So why do we have courts?

00:01:26.228 --> 00:01:30.064
Because without them, people might try to solve problems by

00:01:30.064 --> 00:01:31.429
shouting or fighting.

00:01:31.429 --> 00:01:35.460
Courts help us settle problems peacefully, with rules that are

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.956
the same for everybody.

00:01:37.656 --> 00:01:41.241
So next time you take turns, listen to both sides,

00:01:41.241 --> 00:01:45.472
and tell the truth, you're doing exactly what a court does.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:47.408
Great job, fairness helper!
